# Port-Remote

This document show how to use `port-remote` script to open port for remote connection

--- 

## Instructions

1. Read ptrm table for SSH_HOST, LOCAL_PORT, REMOTE_IP, REMOTE_PORT via command: `cat ~/echo-home/.vim/pages/$(hostname).ptrm.md | head -n -2`

2. Then run : 
- command: `wt  "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" -li -c "port-remote <SSH_HOST> <LOCAL_PORT> <REMOTE_IP> <REMOTE_PORT>"`

- Example: `wt  "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" -li -c "port-remote llama-ssh-host 8082 127.0.0.1 8082"`
3. Test port open successful: `curl -v http://127.0.0.1:<LOCAL_PORT> 2>&1  | grep -m 1 Established`
